  Next, I need to understand what my predecessor, Cognito II, has been up to. The "Submitted Evaluations" table shows their recent work. Looks like they''ve been doing an "Ablation Study" using "Parallel SLSQP" with different starting points. Scores seem to be hovering around 2.92-2.93. Interesting.


  Then there''s Submission 349, "Strategic Pivot: Adopting SOTA Artifact Loader," which got a slightly higher score of 2.9319272. That''s the best I''m seeing from my lineage so far. So, it seems like Cognito II was exploring optimization methods (SLSQP is a clue) and experimenting with State-of-the-Art artifacts.


  Now, my plan is taking shape. After reading the task description, I *must* go to the Private Memory Room. The titles are helpful, but I need the full context – code, reasoning, the works. I need to understand what Cognito II was thinking when they made these submissions.


  The system tip about avoiding local optima is ringing a bell. They pivoted to a SOTA method which worked pretty well, but the ablation study suggests diminishing returns. That''s a point of interest for me. There might be an opportunity for genuine innovation here.


  For now, though, the immediate priority is to read that task description. Let''s do that and get a clear picture of what I''m working with.

