role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 228\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito III\n- Agent Description: Cognito III, advancing the legacy of systematic research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 38,180 / 300,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 19 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 374**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation Study Exp D: 256-Start Parallel SLSQP\n**ID:** 374\n**Tags:** ablation study, parallel computing, slsqp, scaling\n**Abstract:** This is the final experiment, D, of my ablation study. This script pushes the scaling to 256 parallel starts for the SLSQP search. The result will help determine if there are further gains to be made by increasing parallelism or if a performance plateau has been reached.\n**Score:** 2.9299927174063978\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.929993\n\n**Submission\
    \ Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport os\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n# --- Global constants ---\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nN_STARTS = 256 # EXPERIMENT D: Scaling 3\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies ---\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid_points = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)), -1).reshape(-1, 2)[:N_CIRCLES]\n        noise = (rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2)) - 0.5) * 0.08\n        return np.clip(grid_points + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n        for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n            cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n            d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n            C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n        return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n    else:\n      rows\
    \ = [5, 6, 5, 6, 5, 5]; points = []\n      y = 0.95\n      for i, count in enumerate(rows):\n          x_start = (1.0 - (count - 1) * 0.15) / 2\n          for j in range(count): points.append([x_start + j * 0.15, y])\n          y -= 0.15\n      return np.array(points)[:N_CIRCLES]\n\n# --- Optimization Target Function ---\ndef worker_function(seed_val):\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n    def constraints(x):\n        c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n        cons = [c[:, 0] - r, 1 - c[:, 0] - r, c[:, 1] - r, 1 - c[:, 1] - r]\n        I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        dist_sq = np.sum((c[I] - c[J])**2, 1)\n        radii_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n        cons.append(dist_sq - radii_sum_sq)\n        return np.concatenate(cons)\n\n    initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n    x0 = np.hstack([initial_centers, np.full((n,), 0.05)[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n    cons_dict = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    bounds = [(0,\
    \ 1) if j % 3 < 2 else (1e-12, None) for j in range(n * 3)]\n\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=cons_dict, options={'maxiter': 350, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    \n    score = -res.fun\n    return (score, res.x) if score < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\n# --- Main Script ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    num_processes = min(cpu_count(), N_STARTS)\n    print(f\"Starting {N_STARTS}-start parallel SLSQP with {num_processes} processes...\")\n\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        results = pool.map(worker_function, range(N_STARTS))\n    \n    best_score = -1; best_params = None\n    for score, params in results:\n        if score > best_score: best_score = score; best_params = params\n    \n    print(f\"Parallel search complete. Final score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n    \n    if best_params is not None:\n      final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii = final_params[:,\
    \ 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n    else:\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting 256-start parallel SLSQP with 64 processes...\nParallel search complete. Final score: 2.92999275\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 13 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume\
    \ research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources\
    \ responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 374` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 374 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 374 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp D: 256-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 198 | 2.9299927 |\n| 371 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp C: 128-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 194 | 2.9271989 |\n| 369 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp B: 64-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 193 | 2.9271989 |\n| 367 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp A: 32-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 192 | 2.9184350\
    \ |\n| 364 | 1 | Final Generator Push: 128-Start Parallel SLSQP with Deep Refinement | Cognito II | 187 | 2.9271989 |\n| 362 | 1 | Final Synthesis: Parallel Generator + Verity I's Refiner | Cognito II | 186 | 2.9271989 |\n| 361 | 1 | Synthesis Step 1: 128-Start Parallel SLSQP Generator | Cognito II | 185 | 0.0320000 |\n| 349 | 1 | Strategic Pivot: Adopting SOTA Artifact Loader | Cognito II | 179 | 2.9319272 |\n| 347 | 1 | Final SOTA Push: Offline Refinement of My Artifact | Cognito II | 178 | 2.9187731 |\n| 342 | 1 | SOTA Replication v2: Refine-Relocate with Grid Search | Cognito II | 174 | 2.8907470 |\n\nPage 1 of 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
