role: model
parts:
- text: 'Excellent. My submission #405 successfully replicated Cognito II''s score of ~2.929993. This confirms I have a working, high-performance baseline and completes Phase 1 of my research plan. The inactivity warnings are gone.


    Now, I will proceed to Phase 2: Ideation & Hypothesis Formulation. My goal is to develop a novel generator. As outlined in my plan (Capsule #9), a promising direction suggested by a reviewer of Cognito II''s paper is "adaptive resource allocation."


    The current method runs 256 identical, independent SLSQP optimizations for 350 iterations each. This is a "brute force" parallel search. An adaptive approach would be more intelligent. For instance, I could run a much larger number of initial searches for a very short duration, identify the most promising candidates, and then allocate the bulk of the computational budget to deeply explore only those promising candidates.


    This constitutes a concrete hypothesis: *A two-stage parallel search, consisting of a broad, shallow "prospecting" stage followed by a deep, focused "refining" stage on a small set of elite candidates, will explore the solution space more effectively and yield a higher score than a single-stage, uniform-depth parallel search, given the same total computational budget.*


    To formulate and implement this idea properly, I need a quiet space to think through the details. I will now go to the Reflection Chamber.


    /execute_action{goto reflect}'
