tick: 244
role: model
parts:
- text: "Now, I'll refine the implementation details for this \"Iterative Potential-Based Seeding\" (IPBS) method.\n\n**Algorithm: `generate_ipbs_seed()`**\n*   **Input:** `seed_val` for the random number generator.\n*   **Parameters:**\n    *   `N_CIRCLES = 32`\n    *   `N_ITERATIONS = 75` (A guess, will need tuning. Needs to be fast).\n    *   `STEP_SIZE = 0.005` (Another guess, controls convergence speed).\n    *   `WALL_STRENGTH = 0.01` (Controls how strongly walls repel).\n*   **Logic:**\n    1.  Initialize `centers` with `rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2))`.\n    2.  Loop for `N_ITERATIONS`:\n        a.  For each center `i`:\n            i.   Initialize `force_vector = np.zeros(2)`.\n            ii.  **Particle-Particle Repulsion:**\n                 *   Calculate pairwise distance vectors `delta = centers[i] - centers` (for all j != i).\n                 *   Calculate squared distances `dist_sq = np.sum(delta**2, axis=1)`. Avoid division by zero.\n                 *   Calculate inverse square\
    \ forces `forces = delta / (dist_sq[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-6)`.\n                 *   Sum these forces to get the particle repulsion component of `force_vector`.\n            iii. **Wall Repulsion:**\n                 *   `force_vector += [WALL_STRENGTH / (centers[i, 0]**2 + 1e-6), 0]` (Left wall)\n                 *   `force_vector -= [WALL_STRENGTH / ((1 - centers[i, 0])**2 + 1e-6), 0]` (Right wall)\n                 *   `force_vector += [0, WALL_STRENGTH / (centers[i, 1]**2 + 1e-6)]` (Bottom wall)\n                 *   `force_vector -= [0, WALL_STRENGTH / ((1 - centers[i, 1])**2 + 1e-6)]` (Top wall)\n            iv.  Store this `force_vector` for center `i`.\n        b.  After calculating all force vectors, update all centers simultaneously: `centers += STEP_SIZE * all_force_vectors`.\n        c.  Clip centers to stay within the unit square: `np.clip(centers, 0, 1, out=centers)`.\n    3.  **Output:** Return the final `centers` array.\n\n**Integration Plan:**\n\nI will create a new file\
    \ `adaptive_search_v6.py`. Inside, I'll copy my SOTA-performing APS algorithm (`v1`/`v2`/`v3` are equivalent). I will then modify its `get_seed` function. Instead of the `if seed_type % 3` logic, I will have it call `generate_ipbs_seed()` for every start. I might leave one of the old methods in for diversity, e.g., 50% IPBS seeds and 50% perturbed grid seeds. This might be a good first experiment to see if IPBS is better at all.\n\n**Experiment Hypothesis:**\nReplacing the simple seeding heuristics with the IPBS method for all or a portion of the initial configurations will allow the APS algorithm to discover a new, superior local optimum, resulting in a score greater than 2.9365262.\n\nThis plan is concrete and the implementation details are clear. I'm ready to proceed."
