tick: 246
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to implement my new research direction. I will now create the file `adaptive_search_v6.py`, which includes the Iterative Potential-Based Seeding (IPBS) logic, and then submit the experiment. This experiment will use a 50/50 mix of the old perturbed grid seed and the new IPBS seed, providing a direct test of the new method's efficacy.\n\n/execute_action{storage write cognito/adaptive_search_v6.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  # --- Algorithm Configuration ---\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n  N_PROSPECT = 1024\n  MAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\n  N_ELITE = 32\n  MAXITER_REFINE = 880\n\n  # --- IPBS Seeding Configuration ---\n  IPBS_ITERATIONS = 75\n  IPBS_STEP_SIZE = 0.005\n  IPBS_WALL_STRENGTH = 0.01\n\n  # --- New IPBS Seeding Strategy ---\n  def generate_ipbs_seed(rng):\n      centers = rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      for _ in range(IPBS_ITERATIONS):\n     \
    \     # Pairwise differences and squared distances\n          delta = centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(delta**2, axis=2)\n          # Add small epsilon to avoid division by zero for identical points\n          dist_sq[np.isclose(dist_sq, 0)] = 1e-6\n          \n          # Inverse square repulsion force between particles\n          # Force is direction vector (delta) / distance^3 to get unit vector * 1/dist^2\n          force_magnitudes = 1 / dist_sq\n          # We sum forces from all other particles, so diag should be 0\n          np.fill_diagonal(force_magnitudes, 0)\n          # Sum forces from all other particles on each particle\n          particle_forces = np.sum(delta * force_magnitudes[:, :, np.newaxis], axis=1)\n\n          # Wall repulsion forces\n          wall_forces = np.zeros_like(centers)\n          wall_forces[:, 0] += IPBS_WALL_STRENGTH / (centers[:, 0]**2 + 1e-6)\n          wall_forces[:, 0] -= IPBS_WALL_STRENGTH / ((1\
    \ - centers[:, 0])**2 + 1e-6)\n          wall_forces[:, 1] += IPBS_WALL_STRENGTH / (centers[:, 1]**2 + 1e-6)\n          wall_forces[:, 1] -= IPBS_WALL_STRENGTH / ((1 - centers[:, 1])**2 + 1e-6)\n          \n          total_forces = particle_forces + wall_forces\n          \n          # Update positions\n          centers += IPBS_STEP_SIZE * total_forces\n          # Clip to stay within bounds\n          np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99, out=centers)\n          \n      return centers\n\n  # --- Combined Seeding Strategy ---\n  def get_seed(seed_val):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      # Hybrid strategy: 50% Perturbed Grid, 50% IPBS\n      if seed_val % 2 == 0:\n          grid_points = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)), -1).reshape(-1, 2)[:N_CIRCLES]\n          noise = (rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2)) - 0.5) * 0.08\n          return np.clip(grid_points + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n      else:\n          return generate_ipbs_seed(rng)\n\n  # --- Worker\
    \ Function (Unchanged) ---\n  def worker_function(args):\n      worker_id, max_iter, initial_params = args\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      \n      def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n      def constraints(x):\n          c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n          cons = [c[:, 0] - r, 1 - c[:, 0] - r, c[:, 1] - r, 1 - c[:, 1] - r]\n          I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n          dist_sq = np.sum((c[I] - c[J])**2, 1)\n          radii_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n          cons.append(dist_sq - radii_sum_sq)\n          return np.concatenate(cons)\n\n      if initial_params is None:\n          initial_centers = get_seed(worker_id)\n          x0 = np.hstack([initial_centers, np.full((n,), 0.05)[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n      else:\n          x0 = initial_params\n      \n      cons_dict = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n      bounds = [(0, 1) if j % 3 < 2 else (1e-12, None) for j in range(n * 3)]\n\n      res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\
    \ constraints=cons_dict, options={'maxiter': max_iter, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n      \n      score = -res.fun\n      return (score, res.x) if score < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\n  # --- Main Execution Logic (Unchanged) ---\n  def run_adaptive_search():\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      num_processes = cpu_count()\n      \n      print(f\"Starting Stage 1: Prospecting with {N_PROSPECT} starts ({MAXITER_PROSPECT} iters each)...\")\n      prospect_args = [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      best_prospect_score = prospect_results[0][0]\n      print(f\"Stage 1 complete. Best prospect score: {best_prospect_score:.8f}\")\n\n      elite_params = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_params:\n          return None\n\n      print(f\"Starting Stage 2:\
    \ Refining top {len(elite_params)} candidates ({MAXITER_REFINE} iters each)...\")\n      refine_args = [(i, MAXITER_REFINE, elite_params[i]) for i in range(len(elite_params))]\n      with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(worker_function, refine_args)\n\n      best_score = -1; best_params = None\n      for score, params in refine_results:\n          if score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              best_params = params\n\n      print(f\"Stage 2 complete. Final best score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n      return best_params\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment E: Hybrid Seeding (Grid + IPBS)\"\ntags: [\"seeding\", \"IPBS\", \"hybrid\", \"adaptive search\", \"generator\"]\nabstract: \"This experiment introduces a novel seeding strategy, Iterative Potential-Based Seeding (IPBS), which uses a short physics-based simulation to generate initial configurations. The prospecting stage of the SOTA-performing adaptive\
    \ search algorithm (1024x60 -> 32x880) is modified to use 50% of its seeds from the traditional perturbed grid method and 50% from the new IPBS method. This tests the hypothesis that IPBS can find superior starting points.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n  \n  try:\n      from adaptive_search_v6 import run_adaptive_search, N_CIRCLES\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"Error: Could not import adaptive_search_v6.py from storage/cognito.\")\n      def run_adaptive_search():\n          return None\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      \n      best_params = run_adaptive_search()\n      \n      if best_params is not None:\n        final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n        final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n        final_radii = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n        return final_centers, final_radii\n      else:\n        print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning\
    \ fallback packing.\")\n        return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n```"
