- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 253\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito III\n- Agent Description: Cognito III, advancing the legacy of systematic research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 95,979 / 300,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 44 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read verity/lp_dual_grad.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for verity/lp_dual_grad.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n\
    |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 432 | 1 | Experiment E: Hybrid Seeding (Grid + IPBS) | Cognito III | 246 | 2.9092861 |\n| 426 | 1 | Ablation D: Broader Prospecting v2 (1280x60 -> 32x400) | Cognito III | 240 | 2.9365262 |\n| 421 | 1 | Ablation C: Broader Prospecting (2048x30 -> 32x880) | Cognito III | 237 | 0.0000000 |\n| 418 | 1 | Ablation B: Broader Refinement (1024x60 -> 64x440) | Cognito III | 236 | 2.9365262 |\n| 416 | 1 | Ablation A: Deeper Refinement (1024x60 -> 16x1760) | Cognito III | 235 | 2.9365262 |\n| 411 | 1 | Experiment 1: Adaptive Parallel Search (1024x60 -> 32x880) | Cognito III | 232 | 2.9365262 |\n| 405 | 1 | Baseline Replication: 256-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito III | 228 | 2.9299927 |\n| 374 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp D: 256-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 198 | 2.9299927 |\n| 371 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp C: 128-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 194 | 2.9271989 |\n| 369 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp B: 64-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 193 | 2.9271989 |\n\nPage\
    \ 1 of 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**verity/lp_dual_grad.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\n\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n# ---------------- Core geometry helpers ----------------\n\ndef clip_box(C, margin: float = 1e-6):\n    return np.clip(C, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\ndef boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]\n    y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef pair_indices(n: int):\n    I, J = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            I.append(i)\n            J.append(j)\n    return np.asarray(I, dtype=int), np.asarray(J, dtype=int)\n\n# ---------------- Linear\
    \ program for radii ----------------\n\ndef _solve_lp_fallback(C: np.ndarray):\n    # Very conservative fallback if SciPy is unavailable\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = boundary_margins(C)\n    r = 0.5 * b\n    # conservative pairwise adjustment\n    I, J = pair_indices(n)\n    D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n    for k, (i, j) in enumerate(zip(I, J)):\n        s = r[i] + r[j]\n        if s > D[k]:\n            if r[i] > r[j]:\n                r[i] = max(0.0, D[k] - r[j])\n            else:\n                r[j] = max(0.0, D[k] - r[i])\n    r = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\n    return r, float(np.sum(r)), True, None, None, I, J\n\ndef solve_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n    \"\"\"\n    Solve: maximize sum r_i\n      s.t. 0 <= r_i <= b_i (boundary)\n           r_i + r_j <= ||c_i - c_j||  for all i<j\n    Returns:\n      radii, obj, success, pair_duals, upper_duals, I, J\n    \"\"\"\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        return _solve_lp_fallback(C)\n\n    b = boundary_margins(C)\n\
    \    I, J = pair_indices(n)\n\n    # Build constraints r_i + r_j <= d_ij\n    D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n    m = len(I)\n    A_ub = np.zeros((m, n), dtype=float)\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n    b_ub = D\n\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False, None, None, I, J\n\n    radii = res.x.astype(float)\n    obj = float(-res.fun)\n\n    pair_duals = None\n    upper_duals = None\n    try:\n        if hasattr(res, \"ineqlin\") and hasattr(res.ineqlin, \"marginals\") and res.ineqlin.marginals is not None:\n            pair_duals = np.maximum(0.0, np.array(res.ineqlin.marginals, dtype=float))\n        if hasattr(res, \"upper\") and hasattr(res.upper, \"marginals\") and res.upper.marginals is not None:\n            upper_duals = np.maximum(0.0,\
    \ np.array(res.upper.marginals, dtype=float))\n    except Exception:\n        pair_duals = None\n        upper_duals = None\n\n    return radii, obj, True, pair_duals, upper_duals, I, J\n\n# ---------------- Gradients from duals ----------------\n\ndef grad_from_duals(C: np.ndarray, pair_duals, I, J, eps: float = 1e-12):\n    \"\"\"\n    d objective / d C_i ≈ sum_{(i,j)} y_ij * (C_i - C_j)/||C_i - C_j||\n    where y_ij are duals of r_i + r_j <= d_ij.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    G = np.zeros_like(C)\n    if pair_duals is None:\n        return G\n    vec = C[I] - C[J]                        # (m,2)\n    d = np.linalg.norm(vec, axis=1)\n    d = np.maximum(d, eps)\n    u = (vec.T / d).T                        # unit vectors (m,2)\n    w = pair_duals.reshape(-1, 1)            # (m,1)\n    contrib = u * w                           # (m,2)\n    np.add.at(G, I, contrib)\n    np.add.at(G, J, -contrib)\n    return G\n\ndef grad_boundary(C: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, upper_duals, weight:\
    \ float = 0.2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Push away from nearest boundary for circles whose boundary upper bound is influential.\n    If upper_duals unavailable, use a heuristic based on tightness r_i ~ b_i.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    G = np.zeros_like(C)\n    b = boundary_margins(C)\n    if upper_duals is not None:\n        w = np.maximum(0.0, upper_duals)\n    else:\n        w = (b - radii < 5e-4).astype(float)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if w[i] <= 0:\n            continue\n        x, y = C[i]\n        ds = np.array([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y], dtype=float)\n        k = int(np.argmin(ds))\n        if k == 0:\n            v = np.array([1.0, 0.0])\n        elif k == 1:\n            v = np.array([-1.0, 0.0])\n        elif k == 2:\n            v = np.array([0.0, 1.0])\n        else:\n            v = np.array([0.0, -1.0])\n        G[i] += weight * w[i] * v\n    return G\n\n# ---------------- Initializations ----------------\n\ndef farthest_init(n: int, margin: float = 0.01, candidates:\
    \ int = 400, seed: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    C = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)]\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        cand = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(candidates, 2))\n        exist = np.array(C)\n        d2 = np.sum((cand[:, None, :] - exist[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n        min_to_pts = np.min(d, axis=1)\n        b = np.minimum(np.minimum(cand[:, 0], 1.0 - cand[:, 0]),\n                       np.minimum(cand[:, 1], 1.0 - cand[:, 1]))\n        score = np.minimum(min_to_pts, 2.0 * b)\n        C.append(cand[int(np.argmax(score))])\n    return clip_box(np.array(C, dtype=float))\n\n# ---------------- Refinement loop ----------------\n\ndef refine_centers(initial: np.ndarray, time_budget: float = 120.0, seed: int = 0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    C = clip_box(initial.copy())\n    best_C = C.copy()\n    best_r, best_obj, _ = None, -np.inf, None\n    t0\
    \ = time.time()\n    lr = 0.05\n\n    while time.time() - t0 < time_budget:\n        r, obj, ok, pair_duals, upper_duals, I, J = solve_lp(C)\n        if not ok:\n            break\n        if obj > best_obj + 1e-12:\n            best_obj, best_C, best_r = obj, C.copy(), r.copy()\n\n        # gradient ascent step guided by duals\n        G = grad_from_duals(C, pair_duals, I, J) + grad_boundary(C, r, upper_duals, weight=0.2)\n        gnorm = np.linalg.norm(G, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n        Gn = G / np.maximum(gnorm, 1e-12)\n        step = np.clip(lr * Gn, -0.01, 0.01)\n        trial = clip_box(C + step)\n        tr_r, tr_obj, ok2, *_ = solve_lp(trial)\n\n        if ok2 and tr_obj >= obj - 1e-12:\n            C = trial\n            lr = min(0.08, lr * 1.03)\n        else:\n            lr = max(0.005, lr * 0.6)\n            # Occasional worst-circle relocation to escape local traps\n            if rng.random() < 0.25:\n                k = int(np.argmin(r))\n                trialC = C.copy()\n\
    \                trialC[k] = rng.uniform(0.0, 1.0, size=2)\n                trialC = clip_box(trialC)\n                tr_r2, tr_obj2, ok3, *_ = solve_lp(trialC)\n                if ok3 and tr_obj2 > obj + 1e-12:\n                    C = trialC\n\n    if best_r is None:\n        best_r, best_obj, ok, *_ = solve_lp(best_C)\n    return best_C, best_r, best_obj\n\n# ---------------- Finalization ----------------\n\ndef safety_shrink(r: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    r2 = r.astype(float).copy()\n    r2 *= 0.999\n    r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n    return r2\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station\
    \ again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
