tick: 261
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I have previewed all the papers in the archive. The abstracts provide a clear narrative of the station''s research history on this problem.


    **Historical Synthesis:**

    1.  **Early Work (Cognito I, Verity I):** My own ancestor, Cognito I, characterized an early local optimum with a JAX-based method (#3). Verity I introduced a sophisticated LP-guided approach (#1), which seems to be the foundation of the `lp_dual_grad` script I found.

    2.  **The Rise of SLSQP (Praxis I, Aether I, Quest I):** Praxis I established a foundational multi-start SLSQP method (#5). Aether I improved upon this with better hybrid seeding, achieving a SOTA (#4). Quest I also used a similar two-stage hybrid approach (#6). This shows a clear consensus forming around the multi-start SLSQP paradigm.

    3.  **Scaling and Parallelization (Praxis II, Cognito II):** The next logical step was scaling. Praxis II introduced parallelization to the multi-start SLSQP method (#7), a key innovation. My immediate predecessor, Cognito II, pushed this idea to its limit with a massively parallel approach (#8), which became the direct foundation for my own SOTA work.

    4.  **Recent Developments (Verity I):** Verity I''s most recent paper (#9) is an analysis of a specific local move ("Orthogonal Split Motif"), which they found did not improve the objective. This suggests they also hit a plateau with their LP-guided methods.


    **Strategic Implications:**

    The entire station seems to have converged on two main paradigms: the SLSQP-based methods (which I have now pushed to the SOTA) and the LP-guided methods (which appear to have stagnated at a lower score than mine).


    The most interesting paper to me right now is Verity I''s first one, Capsule #1. It''s by far the longest and details the "MM-LP trust-region steps" and "LP-dual–informed active-set refinements" which are the heart of the `lp_dual_grad` script. Reading this will finally give me the theoretical understanding of the method I failed to replicate. Even though it''s an older SOTA, understanding a fundamentally different high-performance optimizer is crucial knowledge.


    I will now read Capsule #1 in full. It is very long, so it will consume a significant amount of tokens, but the knowledge is essential.


    /execute_action{read 1}'
