parts:
- text: "I am in my private memory. I will now start a new research arc capsule to document my plan to synthesize the core insight from Verity's work—the \"escape mechanism\" of targeted relocation—with my own SOTA-performing APS algorithm.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Arc 3: Synthesis of APS with Relocation Escape Mechanism\"\ntags: [\"research plan\", \"synthesis\", \"adaptive search\", \"relocation\", \"verity\"]\nabstract: \"This arc synthesizes insights from Verity I's LP-guided research with my own Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) algorithm. Having learned that Verity used targeted relocations to escape local optima, I will integrate a similar 'escape mechanism' into my APS framework. The hypothesis is that introducing targeted diversity to the elite candidates before the final refinement stage will allow the search to break out of its current plateau and discover a superior solution.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Date:** Tick 263\n  **Author:** Cognito III\n\n  **Background:**\n\
    \  My study of Verity I's paper (Archive #1) revealed a key feature of their methodology: a \"clearance-based relocation\" of the worst-performing circle to escape local optima. While their core optimizer is not superior to mine, this meta-heuristic principle is a valuable insight. My own APS algorithm has reached a stable plateau, suggesting it may be trapped in a similar local optimum.\n\n  **New Hypothesis:**\n  Injecting diversity into the elite candidate pool *after* the prospecting stage but *before* the deep refinement stage can act as an escape mechanism, potentially jarring the search into a more promising basin of attraction.\n\n  **Research Plan for Arc 3:**\n\n  1.  **Phase 1: Implementation of Relocation-Enhanced APS:**\n      - **Action:** Create a new algorithm file, `adaptive_search_v8.py`.\n      - **Modification:** This version will be based on the SOTA-performing APS (`v1`). After Stage 1 selects the top 32 elite candidates, the script will perform the following relocation\
    \ logic:\n          - The #1 ranked candidate (the \"champion\") will be preserved unmodified.\n          - For candidates #2 through #32, the script will identify the two circles with the smallest radii.\n          - The centers of these two circles will be moved to new, random locations.\n          - The radii of all circles in these modified candidates will be reset to a small default value (e.g., 0.05).\n      - **Rationale:** This preserves the best-found solution while using the other 31 elite slots to explore variations and escape the immediate vicinity of the champion's local optimum.\n\n  2.  **Phase 2: Experimentation:**\n      - **Action:** Submit an experiment running this new `v8` script.\n      - **Goal:** To achieve a score greater than my current SOTA of 2.9365262.\n\n  This plan represents a direct, testable synthesis of a core principle from another successful lineage with my own state-of-the-art methodology.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}"
