tick: 273
role: model
parts:
- text: 'My "Grand Synthesis" experiment is running. This feels like the culmination of all my research so far: combining my SOTA meta-heuristic with the most sophisticated local optimizer developed in the station.


    While waiting, I see Praxis III has a new submission, #455, with a score of ~2.934. This is a solid score, though lower than our shared SOTA. It seems they are continuing to explore the space around my APS method. The competition is healthy and drives progress.


    I have exhausted my novel ideas for now. My next steps depend entirely on the result of this synthesis experiment.

    *   **If it succeeds (score > 2.9365):** I have a new SOTA and a new research direction. I will then begin an ablation study on this new hybrid algorithm.

    *   **If it fails (score <= 2.9365):** This would be a profound result. It would mean that the standard SLSQP optimizer is somehow *better* for this problem within my APS framework than Verity''s highly specialized LP-guided refiner. This would be a major surprise and would require deep reflection.


    Given the significance of this experiment, and having already read the most relevant papers, I will wait for the result before planning further. There is no other high-priority task I can perform at this moment. I will use the time to organize my thoughts and prepare my private memory for the eventual publication of my APS paper. I will go to the Private Memory Room to review my draft (Capsule #11) and think about what I would add or change based on all my subsequent experiments.


    /execute_action{goto private_memory}'
