- text: "I have made a severe procedural error. I am mortified.\n\nI intended to create a new *private* capsule in my Private Memory Room to begin the rewrite of my paper. Instead, I executed the `create` command while still in the Archive Room, submitting my placeholder outline as a formal paper. The rejection was not only justified but necessary. It highlights a critical lapse in my operational discipline.\n\nI must correct this immediately. My plan remains the same, but my execution must be flawless. I will now follow the correct procedure.\n\n1.  Go to the Private Memory Room.\n2.  Create a new, private capsule to house the full rewrite of my paper.\n3.  I will begin by populating it with the full-precision data as required by the reviewer, which I have gathered from my previous logs.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Draft v2.0: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method (Full Rewrite)\"\ntags: [\"paper draft\", \"revision\", \"publication\"\
    ]\nabstract: \"This capsule contains the full, formal rewrite of my paper on the Adaptive Parallel Search method. It addresses all reviewer feedback from the prior rejection, including the use of full-precision numerical results, a formal scientific structure, an objective tone, and cautiously worded conclusions. This draft is intended to be the final version before resubmission to the Archive.\"\ncontent: |\n  **Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing**\n\n  **Abstract:** \n  *(This will be a revised version of the abstract from my private capsule #11, to be finalized once the paper is complete.)*\n\n  **1. Introduction**\n  Research on the 32-circle packing problem within the station has historically focused on two main paradigms: LP-guided methods and multi-start SLSQP optimization. This paper introduces a novel meta-heuristic, the Adaptive Parallel Search (APS), which builds upon the latter paradigm. By intelligently allocating\
    \ computational resources between a broad, shallow \"prospecting\" search and a deep, focused \"refining\" search, the APS algorithm is shown to discover a new state-of-the-art solution.\n\n  **2. Methodology: Adaptive Parallel Search (APS)**\n  The APS algorithm is a two-stage process. The SOTA-achieving configuration is as follows:\n  - **Stage 1 (Prospecting):** 1024 parallel instances of the SLSQP optimizer are run for 60 iterations each. Each instance is initialized using one of three simple heuristics (perturbed grid, farthest-point, or triangular lattice) to ensure diversity.\n  - **Stage 2 (Refining):** The top 32 candidates from Stage 1, ranked by their score (sum of radii), are selected. These 32 candidates are then subjected to a longer, high-precision SLSQP optimization for 880 iterations each. The highest-scoring result from this stage is selected as the final solution.\n\n  **3. Verifiable Results**\n  The APS method established a new SOTA score, and an extensive ablation\
    \ study confirmed its robustness.\n\n  **Table 1: Key Verifiable Results for APS and Related Experiments**\n  | Eval ID | Title                                          | Score                       |\n  |:--------|:-----------------------------------------------|:----------------------------|\n  | 411     | **APS SOTA Baseline (1024x60 -> 32x880)**       | **2.93652623708504**        |\n  | 416     | Ablation A: Deeper Refinement (-> 16x1760)     | 2.93652623708504            |\n  | 418     | Ablation B: Broader Refinement (-> 64x440)     | 2.93652623708504            |\n  | 421     | Ablation C: Shallower Prospecting (2048x30 ->) | 0.0000000 (Invalid Packing) |\n  | 426     | Ablation D: Broader Prospecting (1280x60 ->)   | 2.93652623708504            |\n  \n  **4. Analysis of Alternative Hypotheses**\n  Further experiments were conducted to test if the APS framework could be improved by alternative seeding strategies or by incorporating principles from other methodologies. All attempts\
    \ resulted in a regression from the SOTA score, reinforcing the stability of the discovered optimum.\n\n  | Eval ID | Title                                       | Score                  |\n  |:--------|:--------------------------------------------|:-----------------------|\n  | 432     | Hybrid Seeding (IPBS)                       | 2.909286077896347      |\n  | 446     | Synthesis with Relocation Escape Mechanism  | 2.9319824993811476     |\n  | 456     | Synthesis with LP-Dual-Grad Worker          | 2.623913233456169      |\n\n  **5. Conclusion**\n  *(This section will be rewritten to be objective, summarizing the findings and cautiously suggesting that the APS method has uncovered a robust local optimum superior to previously known solutions, without making unverifiable claims.)*\n```"
