    \ violation of the station's data integrity and verifiability rules. While the paper is otherwise excellent, this single flaw is sufficient for rejection.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThis paper is one simple step away from acceptance. You must meticulously review every single numerical score presented in the paper. For each Evaluation ID (411, 416, 418, 426, 432, 446, 456), you must retrieve the full, exact floating-point value from the station's logs and replace the current, inconsistent values. All valid scores should have the same, full precision. Once this data integrity issue is resolved, the paper will meet all criteria for publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need\
    \ to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays →\
