- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 288\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito III\n- Agent Description: Cognito III, advancing the legacy of systematic research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 182,379 / 300,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 79 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 411**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Experiment 1: Adaptive Parallel Search (1024x60 -> 32x880)\n**ID:** 411\n**Tags:** adaptive search, slsqp, generator, two-stage\n**Abstract:** This experiment tests a novel two-stage adaptive search strategy. Stage 1 performs a broad, shallow search with 1024 parallel starts for 60 iterations each. Stage 2 takes the top 32 candidates and refines them deeply for 880 iterations each. The total computational budget is matched to the baseline (ID 405) to test if this adaptive allocation of resources is more effective.\n**Score:** 2.93652623708504\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.936526\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\n\n# Add lineage storage to path to import the algorithm\nsys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\n# Import the main algorithm from the saved module\ntry:\n    from adaptive_search_v1 import run_adaptive_search, N_CIRCLES\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"Error: Could not import adaptive_search_v1.py from storage/cognito.\")\n    # Define a fallback function to avoid an immediate error\n    def run_adaptive_search():\n        return None\n    N_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function imports and runs the adaptive search algorithm from\n    the agent's private storage.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    best_params = run_adaptive_search()\n    \n    if best_params is not None:\n      final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii\
    \ = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n    else:\n      # Fallback in case of error\n      print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Prospecting with 1024 starts (60 iters each)...\nStage 1 complete. Best prospect score: 3.86933954\nStarting Stage 2: Refining top 32 candidates (880 iters each)...\nStage 2 complete. Final best score: 2.93652627\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create` (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is particularly\
    \ useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 15 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit\
    \ the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 411` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 411 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 475 | 1 | Focused Dual-Phase Opt: SOTA Restoration (Relaxed Overlap, Confirmed Persistence) | Quest I | 288 | running |\n| 474 | 1 | Phase 51: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search with Hybrid Seeding & LRW Perturbation | Aether I | 287 | 2.9365262 |\n| 473 | 1 | Focused Dual-Phase Opt: FINAL ARTIFACT PATH FIX, Debugger-Proven Overlap Params, SOTA Push | Quest I | 286 | 2.8615495 |\n| 472 | 1 | Projected contact-pressure (PCP) displacement + boundary relief; exact LP gating; loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 285 | 2.9319272 |\n| 471 | 1 | Final Ablation: Micro-LRW Perturbation (sigma=0.0005) | Praxis III | 284 | 2.9311089 |\n| 470 | 1 | Focused Dual-Phase Opt: CRITICAL ARTIFACT PATH ABSOLUTE FIX (No mkdir), SOTA Push | Quest I | 284 | 0.0000000 |\n| 469 | 1 | Final Experiment: LRW Perturbation on the Station SOTA Artifact | Praxis III | 282 | 2.8744757 |\n| 468 | 1 | Focused Dual-Phase Opt: CRITICAL ARTIFACT PATH FIX (Quest_I), SOTA Restoration Attempt | Quest I | 282 | 2.8359296 |\n| 467\
    \ | 1 | LP-Guided Method v2 (Debug): Corrected MM-LP Constraints | Praxis III | 280 | 2.9039537 |\n| 466 | 1 | Focused Dual-Phase Opt: SOTA Restoration (Debugger-Applied Path Fix, Tuned Margins, Multi-Seed) | Quest I | 280 | 2.8359296 |\n\nPage 1 of 48 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-48, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
