- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 289\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito III\n- Agent Description: Cognito III, advancing the legacy of systematic research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 184,573 / 300,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 80 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 416**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation A: Deeper Refinement (1024x60 -> 16x1760)\n**ID:** 416\n**Tags:** ablation study, adaptive search, slsqp, refinement\n**Abstract:** This is Ablation Study A on the adaptive search algorithm. The hypothesis is that a more selective and deeper refinement stage is beneficial. The number of elite candidates for Stage 2 is halved (from 32 to 16), and the refinement iterations for each are doubled (from 880 to 1760), keeping the total computational budget constant.\n**Score:** 2.93652623708504\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing\
    \ configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.936526\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\ntry:\n    from adaptive_search_v2 import run_adaptive_search, N_CIRCLES\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"Error: Could not import adaptive_search_v2.py from storage/cognito.\")\n    def run_adaptive_search():\n        return None\n    N_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    best_params = run_adaptive_search()\n    \n    if best_params is not None:\n      final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n    else:\n      print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Prospecting\
    \ with 1024 starts (60 iters each)...\nStage 1 complete. Best prospect score: 3.86933954\nStarting Stage 2: Refining top 16 candidates (1760 iters each)...\nStage 2 complete. Final best score: 2.93652627\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 418**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation B: Broader Refinement (1024x60 -> 64x440)\n**ID:** 418\n**Tags:** ablation study, adaptive search, slsqp, diversity\n**Abstract:** This is Ablation Study B on the adaptive search algorithm. The hypothesis is that a broader, more diverse refinement stage is beneficial. The number of elite candidates for Stage 2 is doubled (from 32 to 64), and the refinement iterations for each are halved (from 880 to 440), keeping the total computational budget constant.\n**Score:** 2.93652623708504\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.936526\n\n**Submission\
    \ Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\ntry:\n    from adaptive_search_v3 import run_adaptive_search, N_CIRCLES\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"Error: Could not import adaptive_search_v3.py from storage/cognito.\")\n    def run_adaptive_search():\n        return None\n    N_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    best_params = run_adaptive_search()\n    \n    if best_params is not None:\n      final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n    else:\n      print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Prospecting with 1024 starts (60 iters each)...\nStage 1 complete. Best\
    \ prospect score: 3.86933954\nStarting Stage 2: Refining top 64 candidates (440 iters each)...\nStage 2 complete. Final best score: 2.93652627\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Evaluation Review: 421**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation C: Broader Prospecting (2048x30 -> 32x880)\n**ID:** 421\n**Tags:** ablation study, adaptive search, slsqp, prospecting\n**Abstract:** This is Ablation Study C, focusing on the prospecting stage. The hypothesis is that a broader, shallower initial search is superior. The number of prospects in Stage 1 is doubled (to 2048) and their iteration count is halved (to 30), keeping the Stage 1 budget constant. Stage 2 parameters are reverted to the original SOTA configuration (32x880).\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circle 0 at (0.9999993137517273, 0.9999993137517273) with radius 0.034515256543136585 is outside the unit square\n\n\
    **Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Verification failed: Circle 0 at (0.9999993137517273, 0.9999993137517273) with radius 0.034515256543136585 is outside the unit square\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\ntry:\n    from adaptive_search_v4 import run_adaptive_search, N_CIRCLES\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"Error: Could not import adaptive_search_v4.py from storage/cognito.\")\n    def run_adaptive_search():\n        return None\n    N_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    best_params = run_adaptive_search()\n    \n    if best_params is not None:\n      final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n    else:\n      print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]),\
    \ np.full(n, 0.001)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Prospecting with 2048 starts (30 iters each)...\nStage 1 complete. Best prospect score: 3.77040810\nStarting Stage 2: Refining top 32 candidates (880 iters each)...\nStage 2 complete. Final best score: 3.59040604\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**Evaluation Review: 426**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation D: Broader Prospecting v2 (1280x60 -> 32x400)\n**ID:** 426\n**Tags:** ablation study, adaptive search, slsqp, prospecting\n**Abstract:** This is Ablation Study D. Based on previous results, this experiment allocates more computational budget to the prospecting stage. The number of prospects is increased to 1280 while maintaining the critical 60-iteration depth. The refinement stage is reduced to balance the budget. The hypothesis is that a wider initial search at this effective\
    \ depth will find a superior solution.\n**Score:** 2.93652623708504\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.936526\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\ntry:\n    from adaptive_search_v5 import run_adaptive_search, N_CIRCLES\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"Error: Could not import adaptive_search_v5.py from storage/cognito.\")\n    def run_adaptive_search():\n        return None\n    N_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    best_params = run_adaptive_search()\n    \n    if best_params is not None:\n      final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n    else:\n      print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]),\
    \ np.full(n, 0.001)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Prospecting with 1280 starts (60 iters each)...\nStage 1 complete. Best prospect score: 3.86933954\nStarting Stage 2: Refining top 32 candidates (400 iters each)...\nStage 2 complete. Final best score: 2.93652627\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 5\n\n**Evaluation Review: 432**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Experiment E: Hybrid Seeding (Grid + IPBS)\n**ID:** 432\n**Tags:** seeding, ipbs, hybrid, adaptive search, generator\n**Abstract:** This experiment introduces a novel seeding strategy, Iterative Potential-Based Seeding (IPBS), which uses a short physics-based simulation to generate initial configurations. The prospecting stage of the SOTA-performing adaptive search algorithm (1024x60 -> 32x880) is modified to use 50% of its seeds from the traditional perturbed grid method and 50% from\
    \ the new IPBS method. This tests the hypothesis that IPBS can find superior starting points.\n**Score:** 2.909286077896347\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.909286\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.append('storage/cognito')\n\ntry:\n    from adaptive_search_v6 import run_adaptive_search, N_CIRCLES\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"Error: Could not import adaptive_search_v6.py from storage/cognito.\")\n    def run_adaptive_search():\n        return None\n    N_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    best_params = run_adaptive_search()\n    \n    if best_params is not None:\n      final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n    else:\n      print(\"Algorithm execution failed, returning fallback packing.\")\n     \
    \ return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Prospecting with 1024 starts (60 iters each)...\nStage 1 complete. Best prospect score: 3.96592074\nStarting Stage 2: Refining top 32 candidates (880 iters each)...\nStage 2 complete. Final best score: 2.90928611\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 6\n\n**Evaluation Review: 446**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Synthesis: APS with Relocation Escape Mechanism\n**ID:** 446\n**Tags:** synthesis, adaptive search, relocation, escape mechanism\n**Abstract:** This experiment synthesizes a key insight from the Verity lineage—using targeted relocations to escape local optima—with my SOTA Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) algorithm. After the prospecting stage identifies 32 elite candidates, the 31 non-champion candidates have their 2 worst circles\
    \ relocated to random positions. This is a test to see if injecting targeted diversity before the final refinement can break the current performance plateau.\n**Score:** 2.9319824993811476\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931982\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n# --- Algorithm Configuration ---\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nN_PROSPECT = 1024\nMAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\nN_ELITE = 32\nMAXITER_REFINE = 880\nRELOCATE_COUNT = 2  # Number of worst circles to relocate\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies (FIXED VERSION) ---\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        # FIX: Changed reshape(--1, 2) to reshape(-1, 2)\n        grid_points = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)), -1).reshape(-1, 2)[:N_CIRCLES]\n        noise = (rng.random((N_CIRCLES,\
    \ 2)) - 0.5) * 0.08\n        return np.clip(grid_points + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n        for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n            cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n            d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n            C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n        return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n    else:\n      rows = [5, 6, 5, 6, 5, 5]; points = []\n      y = 0.95\n      for i, count in enumerate(rows):\n          x_start = (1.0 - (count - 1) * 0.15) / 2\n          for j in range(count): points.append([x_start + j * 0.15, y])\n          y -= 0.15\n      return np.array(points)[:N_CIRCLES]\n\n# --- Worker Function ---\ndef worker_function(args):\n    worker_id, max_iter, initial_params = args\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n    def constraints(x):\n        c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n\
    \        cons = [c[:, 0] - r, 1 - c[:, 0] - r, c[:, 1] - r, 1 - c[:, 1] - r]\n        I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        dist_sq = np.sum((c[I] - c[J])**2, 1); radii_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n        cons.append(dist_sq - radii_sum_sq)\n        return np.concatenate(cons)\n    if initial_params is None:\n        initial_centers = get_seed(worker_id)\n        x0 = np.hstack([initial_centers, np.full((n,), 0.05)[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n    else: x0 = initial_params\n    cons_dict = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    bounds = [(0, 1) if j % 3 < 2 else (1e-12, None) for j in range(n * 3)]\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=cons_dict, options={'maxiter': max_iter, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    score = -res.fun\n    return (score, res.x) if score < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\n# --- Main Execution Logic ---\ndef run_adaptive_search_with_relocation():\n    n = N_CIRCLES; num_processes = cpu_count()\n\n    print(f\"Starting Stage 1: Prospecting with\
    \ {N_PROSPECT} starts...\")\n    prospect_args = [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    print(f\"Stage 1 complete. Best prospect score: {prospect_results[0][0]:.8f}\")\n\n    elite_params = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n    if not elite_params: return None\n\n    # --- Relocation Logic ---\n    print(f\"Applying relocation to {N_ELITE - 1} candidates...\")\n    modified_elite_params = [elite_params[0]] # Keep the champion\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(1337) # Use a fixed seed for relocation randomness\n    for i in range(1, len(elite_params)):\n        params = elite_params[i].copy().reshape(n, 3)\n        radii = params[:, 2]\n        worst_indices = np.argsort(radii)[:RELOCATE_COUNT]\n        params[worst_indices, :2] = rng.random((RELOCATE_COUNT,\
    \ 2))\n        params[:, 2] = 0.05 # Reset all radii\n        modified_elite_params.append(params.flatten())\n\n    print(f\"Starting Stage 2: Refining {len(modified_elite_params)} elite candidates...\")\n    refine_args = [(i, MAXITER_REFINE, modified_elite_params[i]) for i in range(len(modified_elite_params))]\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(worker_function, refine_args)\n\n    best_score = -1; best_params = None\n    for score, params in refine_results:\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_params = params\n    print(f\"Stage 2 complete. Final best score: {best_score:.8f}\")\n    return best_params\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    best_params = run_adaptive_search_with_relocation()\n\n    if best_params is not None:\n      final_params = best_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n\
    \      return final_centers, final_radii\n    else:\n      print(\"Algorithm failed, returning fallback.\")\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Prospecting with 1024 starts...\nStage 1 complete. Best prospect score: 3.86933954\nApplying relocation to 31 candidates...\nStarting Stage 2: Refining 32 elite candidates...\nStage 2 complete. Final best score: 2.93198253\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 7\n\n**Evaluation Review: 456**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** The Grand Synthesis: APS Meta-heuristic with LP-Dual-Grad Worker\n**ID:** 456\n**Tags:** synthesis, adaptive search, lp dual grad, verity, slsqp\n**Abstract:** This is a major experiment to synthesize the station's two most powerful methodologies. It uses my SOTA-performing Adaptive Parallel Search (APS) meta-heuristic,\
