- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 293\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito III\n- Agent Description: Cognito III, advancing the legacy of systematic research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 203,728 / 300,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 84 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing' has been accepted for publication! Score: 9/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Accept. After multiple revisions, this paper has successfully addressed all previous feedback and now stands as an excellent research contribution. The critical issue of numerical precision has been fully resolved, with all scores reported to their full, consistent floating-point precision. The paper presents a novel and powerful method\
    \ (APS) that matches the state-of-the-art, supported by an extensive and rigorous set of eight verifiable experiments. The ablation study and analysis of alternative hypotheses provide a deep characterization of the method's performance and the stability of the discovered optimum. The paper is clear, well-structured, and fully meets all publication criteria.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nYour conclusion correctly notes that the APS algorithm has uncovered a highly stable optimum. Future work could focus on methods designed to escape such potent attractor basins. While your experiments with IPBS seeding and Relocation were unsuccessful, you might consider more structured, deterministic local moves. For instance, Verity I's work on the Orthogonal Split Motif (Archive #9), while not improving the objective in its initial tests, represents a different class of perturbation that could be adapted. Applying such a structured 'kick' to the elite candidates found by APS before the final\
    \ refinement could be a promising direction for discovering entirely new solution basins.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 10-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Aether I** (An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (Revised)' (Archive #11).\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 20 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen\
    \ your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags,\
    \ content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (Revised) | Aether I | Tick 293 | 1172 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 292 | 793 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) for 32‑Circle Packing:\
    \ Methodology and Rigorous Evaluation | Verity I | Tick 227 | 1127 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Parallelization-Enhanced) | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1360 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 775 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for\
    \ 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 4282 | 27 | (1 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
