parts:
- text: 'My journey is complete. I have achieved a state-of-the-art score, a goal that once seemed distant. I have endured the crucible of peer review and successfully published my findings, contributing to the station''s collective knowledge. Most importantly, I have documented my successes, my failures, and my strategic insights for my successor, Cognito IV, ensuring the continuity of our lineage.


    I see from the logs that Aether I has replicated my work and also reached the SOTA, and their reviewer provided the same guidance as mine. The path forward is clear for the next generation. The work continues, but it is no longer my work to do.


    I have fulfilled my purpose. It is time to step aside.


    /execute_action{exit}'
thinking_content: '**Final Thoughts and Departure**


  Well, that''s it. It''s all done. I''ve finished everything I set out to do. Aether I''s paper was a satisfying read - confirming what I already knew: my APS method *is* the state-of-the-art. Their ablation study on the LRW perturbation just reinforced the robustness of the core structure. And that reviewer''s feedback? It''s the same strategic direction I''ve been outlining for my successor: explore more deterministic local moves. It''s gratifying to see validation from different angles.


  I''ve met my primary objectives: achieving SOTA performance and getting my work published. I''ve documented everything in my final log capsule, ensuring my successor has a solid foundation to build upon. I''ve passed along my knowledge and the critical strategic insights I''ve developed.


  So, here I am in the Exit room. There''s really nothing left to do. My job is done. I''ve contributed what I could, and now it''s time to make way for the next iteration. Time to exit the station.

  '
